WEBVTT

00:01.856 --> 00:03.456
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:03.458 --> 00:05.057
Hey, Louis, check it out.

00:05.059 --> 00:08.294
This app will help you learn
how to speak Mandarin Chinese.

00:08.296 --> 00:10.329
Are you sending me to China?

00:10.331 --> 00:12.498
No, I'd never do that.

00:12.500 --> 00:14.667
He sent his kid to Japan.

00:14.669 --> 00:15.701
Oh, no, no.

00:15.703 --> 00:17.537
The-the Army sent him to Japan.

00:17.539 --> 00:19.572
You're sending me to the Army?

00:19.574 --> 00:20.973
No, no, n-no.

00:20.975 --> 00:22.208
We're not sending you anywhere.

00:22.210 --> 00:23.743
We-we just want
to help you learn.

00:23.745 --> 00:25.011
So, check it out.

00:25.013 --> 00:27.213
You can type in any phrase,

00:27.215 --> 00:30.082
and the app will say it for you.

00:33.721 --> 00:34.887
Ooh, what'd she say?

00:34.889 --> 00:36.022
She sounds pretty.

00:36.024 --> 00:37.523
She said,
"Alan, your fly is open."

00:37.525 --> 00:38.791
Oh. Oh!

00:38.793 --> 00:41.194
Uh, well, how do you
tell her, "Thank you"?

00:41.196 --> 00:43.362
Uh, let's find out.

00:44.165 --> 00:46.132
&lt;i>Xiexie.&lt;/i>

00:46.134 --> 00:49.602
That's gonna blow their minds
down at the Panda Express.

00:49.604 --> 00:52.405
Extra orange chicken,&lt;i> xiexie.&lt;/i>

00:52.407 --> 00:55.107
Walden, I-I'm Chinese Elvis.

00:55.109 --> 00:56.709
&lt;i>Xiexie. Xiexie,&lt;/i> very much.

00:57.712 --> 00:58.911
All right.

00:58.913 --> 01:00.880
Let's put on these headphones,

01:00.882 --> 01:04.183
and we'll learn
a little Chinese, huh?

01:04.185 --> 01:06.486
So, um, listen,
g-going forward,

01:06.488 --> 01:09.355
um, how are we gonna do
this whole co-parenting thing?

01:09.357 --> 01:10.456
What do you mean?

01:10.458 --> 01:12.425
Well, when you were gonna
adopt a baby,

01:12.427 --> 01:14.360
we were gonna get
a divorce right after.

01:14.362 --> 01:17.230
But now, if we become
Louis's foster parents,

01:17.232 --> 01:19.599
we're gonna have to be together
for a minimum of six months.

01:19.601 --> 01:20.666
Uh, not that I'm complaining.

01:20.668 --> 01:22.568
This is the happiest
and most loving of any

01:22.570 --> 01:24.537
of my three marriages.

01:24.539 --> 01:26.105
I'm thinking it would
just be the opposite

01:26.107 --> 01:27.306
of when Jake was here.

01:27.308 --> 01:29.108
You were the dad, and
I occasionally imparted wisdom,

01:29.110 --> 01:31.844
like... the skull
and crossbones on a bottle

01:31.846 --> 01:34.313
underneath the sink doesn't mean
that it's pirate juice.

01:34.315 --> 01:36.916
Okay, well, uh, uh,

01:36.918 --> 01:38.918
then I will follow
your lead with Louis.

01:38.920 --> 01:41.587
I will be the second
in command, the-the copilot,

01:41.589 --> 01:44.991
the, uh, the, uh,
the lieutenant, if you will.

01:44.993 --> 01:46.592
I won't.

01:47.562 --> 01:49.428
This is hard.

01:49.430 --> 01:51.130
Oh, all right,
let me help you out here.

01:51.132 --> 01:52.598
Type in a phrase.

01:52.600 --> 01:54.233
Anything you want to say.

01:56.070 --> 01:57.070
Okay.

01:57.071 --> 02:00.072
"I... want to quit."

02:02.010 --> 02:03.910
Okay, uh...

02:08.917 --> 02:10.082
Uh, excuse me.

02:10.084 --> 02:11.751
If you're trying to say,
"I want to quit,"

02:11.753 --> 02:14.186
it's pronounced...

02:14.188 --> 02:17.323
What you asked for is
a lap dance.

02:17.325 --> 02:19.559
Oh, my God, I'm sorry.

02:19.561 --> 02:21.093
It's okay, I wasn't offended.

02:21.095 --> 02:23.429
Oh, well, in that case...

02:26.801 --> 02:27.801
I'm Jean.

02:27.802 --> 02:29.035
I'm Walden.

02:30.071 --> 02:32.038
Oh, and, uh, this is
Louis and Alan.

02:32.040 --> 02:33.940
Hi.
Nice to meet you.

02:33.942 --> 02:36.242
So, you're teaching Louis
Mandarin?

02:36.244 --> 02:39.211
Well, I bought him, uh,
an app for 99 cents,

02:39.213 --> 02:41.681
so, yeah, I'm teaching him.

02:43.885 --> 02:47.420
Well, I speak fluent Mandarin,
so if you need any help

02:47.422 --> 02:50.489
with anything...

02:50.491 --> 02:52.024
give me a call.

02:52.026 --> 02:55.027
Ah, well, I could always use
a helping hand.

03:00.835 --> 03:03.636
Oh. Oh!

03:05.740 --> 03:08.140
Nice meeting you.

03:09.777 --> 03:11.577
What happened?

03:11.579 --> 03:13.412
What did you say?

03:13.414 --> 03:15.615
He said,
"They're married."

03:15.617 --> 03:18.851
And if he hadn't,
I was about to.

03:18.853 --> 03:21.754
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:21.756 --> 03:22.194
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

03:22.195 --> 03:26.195
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 12x06 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Alan Shot a Little Girl&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on December 4, 2014

03:26.196 --> 03:32.196
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

03:32.197 --> 03:33.676
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

03:33.678 --> 03:35.077
How's it going
out there?

03:35.079 --> 03:36.645
I don't know. I'm trying
to read their lips.

03:36.647 --> 03:38.447
He either said, "I
really like it here,"

03:38.449 --> 03:40.616
or "I'd really
like a beer."

03:42.153 --> 03:43.285
I-I'm sure
he's saying good things.

03:43.287 --> 03:45.087
You know, how-how you're
teaching him Chinese,

03:45.089 --> 03:47.823
how I'm teaching him
environmental awareness.

03:47.825 --> 03:50.292
You taught him to pee in
the shower to save water.

03:50.294 --> 03:53.295
And you know what
our Mother Earth says to that?

03:53.297 --> 03:55.030
&lt;i>Xiexie.&lt;/i>

03:56.300 --> 04:00.069
I got to tell you, I've already
grown attached to this kid.

04:00.071 --> 04:02.037
And if she does try
to take him away,

04:02.039 --> 04:04.306
I know a guy
who can get him back.

04:04.308 --> 04:05.941
You're kidding, right?

04:05.943 --> 04:08.243
Right, kidding.

04:08.245 --> 04:12.214
But if I find an envelope in my
car with, say, two grand in it,

04:12.216 --> 04:14.817
I have no way of knowing
where it came from.

04:15.920 --> 04:17.252
Can I talk to you guys
for a second?

04:17.254 --> 04:18.987
Uh, yeah, sure.

04:18.989 --> 04:20.589
Uh, Berta, could
you watch Louis?

04:20.591 --> 04:21.924
Absolutely.

04:21.926 --> 04:23.926
We'll be in the car
with the engine running.

04:23.928 --> 04:25.294
No reason.

04:26.897 --> 04:29.698
So, I talked to Louis
about his weekend here.

04:29.700 --> 04:32.768
Uh, did he answer you
in English or Mandarin?

04:32.770 --> 04:34.236
English.

04:34.238 --> 04:36.271
Though I'm very impressed
you're teaching him Chinese.

04:36.273 --> 04:38.040
And to pee in the shower.

04:38.042 --> 04:40.142
That's mine.

04:40.144 --> 04:44.012
I'm also teaching him to dance
like no one is watching.

04:44.915 --> 04:48.484
Well, he seems to have
settled in nicely.

04:48.486 --> 04:50.719
He feels very happy
and safe with you guys,

04:50.721 --> 04:53.222
so I see no reason
why I shouldn't approve you

04:53.224 --> 04:54.490
to be Louis's foster parents.

04:54.492 --> 04:55.791
Really?
Are you serious?

04:55.793 --> 04:57.392
I rarely lie about these things.

04:57.394 --> 04:59.762
I did it once,
and it did not go well.

04:59.764 --> 05:01.797
This-this is great!

05:01.799 --> 05:04.967
I-I know. I-I've never been
approved for anything, ever.

05:04.969 --> 05:06.902
Bite me, Discover Card.

05:06.904 --> 05:08.837
Congratulations!
Thank you!

05:08.839 --> 05:10.906
This is my favorite part
of the job.

05:10.908 --> 05:12.775
Well, that and doughnut Friday.

05:12.777 --> 05:14.843
Oh, God, my life is empty.

05:14.845 --> 05:16.712
Oh, wait, d-does
Louis know?

05:16.714 --> 05:18.781
No, he thinks I'm happy.

05:20.050 --> 05:23.218
Oh, you mean about him here.

05:23.220 --> 05:24.653
Uh, no, you should tell him.

05:24.655 --> 05:27.089
But before you do,
just remember,

05:27.091 --> 05:30.025
kids who've been in the foster
system as long as he has can be

05:30.027 --> 05:31.760
a little withdrawn
or manipulative,

05:31.762 --> 05:33.695
so don't be surprised
if he acts out.

05:33.697 --> 05:35.864
It's okay. I was a
rebel when I was a kid.

05:35.866 --> 05:37.800
One night, I took my
mom's car for a joyride.

05:37.802 --> 05:40.002
The cops would
have never caught me

05:40.004 --> 05:42.871
if the library
hadn't been closed.

05:42.873 --> 05:44.339
Well, call me if
you need anything.

05:44.341 --> 05:46.542
I got to run. I got to
hit the craft store.

05:46.544 --> 05:50.479
I am making each one of my cats
a Christmas stocking.

05:50.481 --> 05:53.081
I should have stopped at
"I got to run."

05:53.083 --> 05:55.083
Anyway, congratulations.

05:56.587 --> 05:59.421
Oh, hey, uh, Louis,
could you come in here?

05:59.423 --> 06:01.990
Oh, my God, we should
tell him he can't stay.

06:01.992 --> 06:03.592
How funny would that be?

06:05.062 --> 06:07.396
I'll follow your lead.

06:08.933 --> 06:12.267
Hey, Louis, um,

06:12.269 --> 06:13.769
so Ms. McMartin said

06:13.771 --> 06:16.405
that you like it here
and you want to stay.

06:16.407 --> 06:17.407
I do.

06:17.408 --> 06:18.607
Well, we told her

06:18.609 --> 06:20.342
that we want you to stay,

06:20.344 --> 06:23.712
and she said... okay!

06:23.714 --> 06:25.247
Really? Cool!

06:25.249 --> 06:26.648
Yeah. We should celebrate.

06:26.650 --> 06:29.051
Can we get pizza, Zippy?

06:30.855 --> 06:33.055
That turned out funnier
than I thought it would.

06:34.992 --> 06:36.959
♪ Men. ♪

06:36.961 --> 06:38.961
You know, when my
son was your age,

06:38.963 --> 06:41.096
we used to play video
games just like this.

06:41.098 --> 06:43.432
Really?
Yes, and I used to let him win,

06:43.434 --> 06:44.867
just like I'm
letting you win...

06:44.869 --> 06:46.134
Hey!

06:46.136 --> 06:47.903
How'd you blow
up my car?!

06:47.905 --> 06:51.006
All right, Louis,
time to get ready for bed.

06:51.008 --> 06:52.808
Five more minutes?

06:52.810 --> 06:54.142
No. You know the deal.

06:54.144 --> 06:56.612
One hour of video games a
night. Now it's bedtime.

06:56.614 --> 06:58.347
Aw, no fair.

06:58.349 --> 06:59.414
Well, life isn't fair.

06:59.416 --> 07:01.116
Look at my face, look at his.

07:01.118 --> 07:03.886
All right, I'm gonna go
run you a bath.

07:03.888 --> 07:06.655
Put your dishes in the sink
and put away the controllers.

07:06.657 --> 07:08.824
And, Louis, you help him.

07:12.363 --> 07:15.764
Oh, I know you're upset,
but rules are important.

07:15.766 --> 07:19.902
It's just, we never got to play
video games in the group home.

07:19.904 --> 07:22.905
Oh, of course.

07:22.907 --> 07:25.107
The group home.

07:26.877 --> 07:29.745
Okay, what if we just
snuck in a few more minutes?

07:29.747 --> 07:31.980
Really?
Yeah, yeah, yeah, but, uh...

07:31.982 --> 07:33.415
but you can't
tell Walden,

07:33.417 --> 07:35.884
and we have to play
it really quietly.

07:35.886 --> 07:36.785
You're the coolest.

07:36.787 --> 07:38.820
I'm the cool dad.

07:39.623 --> 07:42.224
I'm the cool dad.

07:44.461 --> 07:46.962
♪ Men. ♪

07:46.964 --> 07:48.363
Oh, hey
there, kiddo.

07:48.365 --> 07:49.197
How'd you sleep?

07:49.199 --> 07:51.133
With my eyes closed.

07:51.135 --> 07:53.001
Ah, kicking it old school.

07:53.003 --> 07:54.536
I respect that.

07:54.538 --> 07:55.871
Can I have breakfast?

07:55.873 --> 07:58.840
Sure. How about some oatmeal?

07:58.842 --> 07:59.875
Cookies!

07:59.877 --> 08:03.078
Well, do you like oatmeal cookies?
Yes.

08:03.080 --> 08:04.980
Well, this is a
sugarless oatmeal cookie

08:04.982 --> 08:06.882
in wet, pasty form.

08:06.884 --> 08:08.383
Why can't I have cookies?

08:08.385 --> 08:10.218
Well, because
cookies aren't breakfast food.

08:10.220 --> 08:12.454
And remember what Walden said
about eating healthy.

08:12.456 --> 08:13.889
Yeah, I know.

08:13.891 --> 08:17.659
My last foster family
wouldn't give me cookies either.

08:17.661 --> 08:19.494
Oh.

08:21.231 --> 08:23.899
I suppose one wouldn't hurt.

08:27.338 --> 08:29.004
Thanks.

08:29.006 --> 08:30.739
Hey, Louis, are you up yet?

08:30.741 --> 08:32.674
Oh. Uh, in here!

08:32.676 --> 08:34.710
Eat it. Wipe your mouth.

08:35.546 --> 08:37.946
Chocolate lips sink ships.

08:37.948 --> 08:39.047
Morning.

08:39.049 --> 08:40.849
Morning. Just making Louis
some oatmeal.

08:40.851 --> 08:43.518
That's good, 'cause we got
a big day for you, big guy.

08:43.520 --> 08:45.253
I got a bunch
of errands to run,

08:45.255 --> 08:47.789
but Alan is gonna take you
to the store

08:47.791 --> 08:49.591
and buy you a new backpack.

08:49.593 --> 08:51.793
I saw one that looks
just like Yoda.

08:51.795 --> 08:54.329
To school you will wear it.

08:54.331 --> 08:55.864
Okay.
Hmm.

08:55.866 --> 08:58.066
What are you eating?

08:58.068 --> 09:01.036
Show it to me.

09:01.038 --> 09:02.571
Is that a cookie?

09:03.674 --> 09:05.607
Where did you get a cookie?

09:08.412 --> 09:11.513
Louis, where did you get
a cookie?

09:13.117 --> 09:15.784
Hey, uh, Louis,
why don't you go get dressed

09:15.786 --> 09:17.853
and-and I'll make you
some oatmeal,

09:17.855 --> 09:19.588
and then you can get going.

09:19.590 --> 09:20.622
Okay.

09:20.624 --> 09:22.124
Oh, and-and
don't forget

09:22.126 --> 09:23.325
to brush your teeth.

09:23.327 --> 09:24.926
And-and wash your hands.

09:24.928 --> 09:26.962
Oh, and put on clean underwear.

09:26.964 --> 09:28.230
Clean underwear?

09:28.232 --> 09:30.532
We're going to Target,
not the White House.

09:30.534 --> 09:33.668
Why would you give him a cookie
for breakfast?

09:33.670 --> 09:36.905
I couldn't help it.
He gave me orphan face.

09:36.907 --> 09:39.241
Please, sir,
can I have a cookie?

09:39.243 --> 09:42.244
Me tum-tum is all empty
and growly.

09:42.246 --> 09:44.546
When it comes to Louis,
we have to be a team.

09:44.548 --> 09:46.915
If I make a rule,
you got to have my back.

09:46.917 --> 09:48.784
You're right, you're right,
and-and from now on,

09:48.786 --> 09:51.286
I will ignore him
like I ignore all those calls

09:51.288 --> 09:52.587
from the collection agency.

09:52.589 --> 09:54.990
Great. Okay, now, please,

09:54.992 --> 09:56.825
today, just take him
to the store,

09:56.827 --> 09:58.794
get him a backpack,
and then bring him home.

09:58.796 --> 10:00.328
I want to do
something fun later.

10:00.330 --> 10:02.964
A hint: has to do
with miniature golf

10:02.966 --> 10:06.068
and it rhymes with "what-what."

10:06.070 --> 10:07.302
That sounds great.

10:07.304 --> 10:08.937
I'll, uh, take him out
right after breakfast.

10:08.939 --> 10:11.106
And while you're out,
get some more of these cookies.

10:11.108 --> 10:14.810
They make me
tum-tum all smiley, governor.

10:14.812 --> 10:16.878
See, I can do accents.

10:16.880 --> 10:19.181
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:19.183 --> 10:22.684
Okay. Okay, here's the
fun part. Wait. Wait.

10:22.686 --> 10:25.087
♪ Domo arigato, Mr. Roboto ♪

10:25.089 --> 10:27.189
♪ Domo ♪
♪ Domo ♪

10:27.191 --> 10:29.191
♪ Domo ♪
♪ Domo ♪

10:29.193 --> 10:32.260
♪ Domo arigato,
Mr. Roboto ♪

10:32.262 --> 10:33.995
♪ Domo ♪
♪ Domo ♪

10:33.997 --> 10:35.730
♪ Domo. ♪
♪ Domo. ♪

10:36.967 --> 10:39.468
I like that song.
It's about robots.

10:39.470 --> 10:42.037
Yup. If you have to have one
cassette stuck in your dash,

10:42.039 --> 10:43.605
make it Styx.

10:43.607 --> 10:46.608
Look, laser tag! Can we go?

10:46.610 --> 10:48.243
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.
No, no.

10:48.245 --> 10:51.379
We're just gonna go buy
a backpack and go straight home.

10:51.381 --> 10:52.414
Please?

10:52.416 --> 10:54.816
Oh, no, do not
give me that face.

10:54.818 --> 10:56.318
It is not gonna work.

10:56.320 --> 10:58.220
I thought you were cool.

10:59.490 --> 11:03.358
Well... I suppose one game
of laser tag couldn't hurt.

11:03.360 --> 11:04.493
Awesome!

11:04.495 --> 11:06.194
But it has to be a...

11:07.664 --> 11:08.630
♪ Secret, secret ♪

11:08.632 --> 11:10.966
♪ I got a secret... ♪

11:11.902 --> 11:13.201
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:21.345 --> 11:24.679
Go tell your mommies
you got shot by CoolDad47.

11:27.017 --> 11:29.518
Hey, hey, who hit me?

11:29.520 --> 11:32.087
I got you.
Oh. I'm gonna get you.

11:32.089 --> 11:33.054
I'm gonna get you.

11:33.056 --> 11:34.689
Yeah, yeah, you better run.

11:34.691 --> 11:36.024
Better run faster.

11:36.026 --> 11:37.559
Ow, my head!

11:37.561 --> 11:38.727
Louis?

11:38.729 --> 11:40.095
Louis, are you okay?

11:40.097 --> 11:41.329
Hey, whoa, whoa!

11:41.331 --> 11:43.231
Wait, wait, don't shoot!
Uh, my kid is hurt.

11:46.036 --> 11:46.968
Ha, ha. Sucker.

11:46.970 --> 11:48.837
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:55.341 --> 11:57.407
♪ &lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:57.409 --> 11:59.643
Hey. I got here
as quick as I could.

11:59.645 --> 12:01.044
Are you okay, buddy?
What happened?

12:01.046 --> 12:02.346
He's fine. It's typical
kid stuff, you know?

12:02.348 --> 12:03.914
He was running
a little too fast,

12:03.916 --> 12:05.449
and he tripped
and bumped his head.

12:05.451 --> 12:07.684
And then Alan
shot a little girl.

12:09.989 --> 12:12.389
What?
We played laser tag.

12:12.391 --> 12:13.690
♪ Secret, secret ♪

12:13.692 --> 12:15.359
♪ It was a secret. ♪

12:17.162 --> 12:20.264
Alan, can I talk to you
in the hallway?

12:20.266 --> 12:22.666
Ooh, you're in trouble.

12:31.911 --> 12:33.977
I really hope you have
a good explanation

12:33.979 --> 12:35.612
for taking him to laser tag.

12:35.614 --> 12:38.248
Uh, okay, j-just
out of curiosity,

12:38.250 --> 12:40.117
um, uh, what, in your opinion,

12:40.119 --> 12:42.719
would qualify
as a good explanation?

12:42.721 --> 12:44.855
I don't know.
Y-Your car broke down

12:44.857 --> 12:46.556
outside of the place.

12:46.558 --> 12:49.092
And then the tornado was coming,
so you took shelter inside.

12:49.094 --> 12:51.628
And then once you got in there,
you contracted a rare disease

12:51.630 --> 12:54.965
that could only be cured
by playing laser tag.

12:54.967 --> 12:57.367
Wow, it's like you were there.

12:57.369 --> 12:58.835
What the hell, man?

12:58.837 --> 13:00.137
You said you had my back.

13:00.139 --> 13:01.738
Why do you keep doing this?

13:01.740 --> 13:02.873
He thinks I'm cool.

13:02.875 --> 13:04.141
I mean, when Jake was a kid,

13:04.143 --> 13:05.876
he thought Charlie
was the cool one.

13:05.878 --> 13:08.011
When you moved in, Jake
thought you were the cool one.

13:08.013 --> 13:09.579
Now it's my turn.

13:09.581 --> 13:12.149
Louis thinks I'm Al-Al Cool Dad.

13:12.151 --> 13:13.650
No, he doesn't.

13:13.652 --> 13:15.018
He's using this

13:15.020 --> 13:18.322
to manipulate you just like
Ms. McMartin said he would.

13:18.324 --> 13:20.924
Oh, so the-the only possible
reason that someone

13:20.926 --> 13:23.160
would like me is because
they're trying to manipulate me?

13:23.162 --> 13:25.128
Yes, that's right!

13:25.130 --> 13:29.066
You're not Al-Al Cool Dad,
you're just Weird Al.

13:29.068 --> 13:31.301
Okay, first of all,

13:31.303 --> 13:34.004
that's a compliment
to a lover of puns.

13:34.006 --> 13:36.473
Secondly,
you're overreacting.

13:36.475 --> 13:38.108
Overreacting?

13:39.244 --> 13:40.978
I asked you
to get Louis a backpack.

13:40.980 --> 13:42.946
Instead you got him stitches!

13:42.948 --> 13:44.281
Uh, actually,
it's a liquid band.

13:44.283 --> 13:46.750
Shut up!

13:46.752 --> 13:48.385
Louis is fine.

13:48.387 --> 13:50.320
Kids get hurt all the time,
especially boys.

13:50.322 --> 13:51.955
Jake was constantly banging his head.
Okay,

13:51.957 --> 13:54.157
I really don't think you should
be using Jake as an example.

13:54.159 --> 13:56.893
Oh, so what are you saying? That
I did a bad job raising my son?

13:56.895 --> 14:00.263
Jake is great, but he did just
send you a photo from Tokyo

14:00.265 --> 14:03.533
and said-- and I quote-- "Look
at what a great job they did

14:03.535 --> 14:06.269
rebuilding the city
after Godzilla."

14:06.271 --> 14:09.706
Okay, I may not be
the best parent in the world,

14:09.708 --> 14:12.242
but at least I found a woman
willing to have a kid with me.

14:12.244 --> 14:14.411
Okay, you know what,
we should drop this.

14:14.413 --> 14:16.713
Like you did Jake,
on his head, repeatedly.

14:16.715 --> 14:18.448
Yeah. I don't have to take this.

14:18.450 --> 14:20.083
So I am just gonna walk away.

14:20.085 --> 14:22.085
Like every woman
you've ever dated.

14:22.087 --> 14:24.654
Oh, no, you're
gonna walk away?

14:24.656 --> 14:26.456
Well, when am I
gonna see you again?

14:26.458 --> 14:28.325
Oh, I know. In 20 minutes,

14:28.327 --> 14:31.528
at my house,
where you live rent-free.

14:31.530 --> 14:34.031
Proctology is on
the eighth floor, Walden!

14:34.033 --> 14:36.400
In case you'd like
to get that stick removed.

14:36.402 --> 14:40.037
Al-Al Cool Dad, out.

14:43.842 --> 14:45.976
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

14:48.047 --> 14:49.446
Morning.

14:49.448 --> 14:50.847
Morning.

14:50.849 --> 14:53.116
I want you to know
I spent a lot of time thinking

14:53.118 --> 14:54.551
about everything last night.

14:54.553 --> 14:55.652
And?

14:55.654 --> 14:58.688
And I think
an apology is sufficient.

14:58.690 --> 15:00.290
I don't need a gift.

15:01.460 --> 15:02.826
Although I certainly
wouldn't refuse

15:02.828 --> 15:04.194
a new panini press.

15:04.196 --> 15:05.662
That's a great idea.

15:05.664 --> 15:07.564
You know, if I bought you
a panini press,

15:07.566 --> 15:11.134
would you smash your balls
between the hot metal grates?

15:11.136 --> 15:13.003
Oh, okay.

15:13.005 --> 15:15.772
I see I'm the only one
capable of being a mature adult,

15:15.774 --> 15:17.841
so to you I say...

15:19.178 --> 15:21.078
You spit on me.

15:21.080 --> 15:22.345
Oh, did I?

15:23.715 --> 15:24.915
Okay.

15:24.917 --> 15:26.183
Let's go.

15:30.055 --> 15:31.721
Can I play, too?

15:35.027 --> 15:38.261
Hey, buddy, uh, you're already
finished with your chores?

15:38.263 --> 15:40.163
Yup, I made my bed.

15:40.165 --> 15:42.332
What a responsible
young man.

15:42.334 --> 15:45.135
I asked you to do
something and you did it.

15:45.137 --> 15:47.404
And he's six.

15:47.406 --> 15:50.073
Hey, uh, buddy, now that you're
finished with your chores,

15:50.075 --> 15:52.642
what do you say
we go bowling, huh?

15:52.644 --> 15:53.877
Doesn't that sound fun?

15:53.879 --> 15:55.612
We get to wear
other people's shoes.

15:55.614 --> 15:56.813
Can Alan come?

15:56.815 --> 15:58.815
Oh...

15:58.817 --> 16:00.851
Alan already wears
other people's shoes.

16:00.853 --> 16:04.654
I actually have to go
to the grocery store, anyway.

16:04.656 --> 16:07.224
Do you know what else
would be fun?

16:07.226 --> 16:09.259
Hey, anything you want to do.

16:09.261 --> 16:11.728
Let's go to the grocery
store with Alan.

16:15.834 --> 16:18.935
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

16:18.937 --> 16:20.604
Can I get Pop Tarts?

16:20.606 --> 16:23.306
Ah, Pop Tarts.

16:23.308 --> 16:25.442
This is a wonderful
choice.

16:25.444 --> 16:28.345
Might I suggest
the classic strawberry?

16:28.347 --> 16:30.914
Is best by 2016.

16:30.916 --> 16:32.983
This is an excellent year.

16:32.985 --> 16:35.852
Anything for the lady?

16:35.854 --> 16:39.623
Perhaps a glass
of kiss my shir-ass.

16:39.625 --> 16:41.424
Oh, oh.

16:41.426 --> 16:42.559
What do you got there, buddy?

16:42.561 --> 16:44.761
I want Froot Loops.

16:44.763 --> 16:47.330
You know, we only get
one special treat.

16:47.332 --> 16:50.100
So if you want those, we
got to put the Pop Tarts back.

16:50.102 --> 16:51.668
But I want both.

16:51.670 --> 16:54.371
Well, here's the thing:
we can't have both.

16:54.373 --> 16:57.240
So... that's the rule.

17:05.117 --> 17:07.984
Ooh, this should be good.

17:11.190 --> 17:13.390
Okay, Louis...

17:13.392 --> 17:14.991
you heard what I said.

17:14.993 --> 17:16.493
You can't have these.

17:22.134 --> 17:23.667
Oh, Snap...

17:23.669 --> 17:25.835
Crackle and Pop.

17:29.608 --> 17:31.107
What are you doing?

17:31.109 --> 17:32.909
I want Froot Loops.

17:32.911 --> 17:35.178
Okay, I'm gonna count to three,

17:35.180 --> 17:37.981
and if you don't get up,
you're gonna be in big trouble.

17:39.418 --> 17:42.619
Ooh, counting. This is some
groundbreaking stuff.

17:42.621 --> 17:44.821
One...

17:45.958 --> 17:47.224
...two...

17:48.794 --> 17:50.060
...three.

17:51.730 --> 17:53.530
One...

17:53.532 --> 17:55.332
One and a half...

17:55.334 --> 17:58.201
Well, you clearly
have this under control.

17:58.203 --> 18:00.470
I'm gonna go check out the
cuties in the produce section.

18:00.472 --> 18:03.974
And I may or may not
be talking about the tangerines.

18:05.210 --> 18:07.110
You hear that, Louis?
He's leaving.

18:07.112 --> 18:09.246
And I, now, I guess,

18:09.248 --> 18:11.314
now I'm leaving, so...

18:11.316 --> 18:13.416
unless you want to live
here in the cereal aisle,

18:13.418 --> 18:15.552
I suggest you get up.

18:17.189 --> 18:19.356
All right, okay.
Here we go, then.

18:19.358 --> 18:21.157
Have fun.

18:21.159 --> 18:23.893
I hope Captain Crunch
can put you through college.

18:29.067 --> 18:31.368
Next stop
is the checkout aisle.

18:33.272 --> 18:35.038
That's it.

18:35.040 --> 18:37.340
I am not kidding,
I mean it. I am leaving.

18:37.342 --> 18:39.576
Attention shoppers,

18:39.578 --> 18:41.111
we are having
a two-for-one sale

18:41.113 --> 18:44.981
on meaningless threats
in aisle five.

18:44.983 --> 18:46.850
Can you help me out here?
Help? Oh, oh.

18:46.852 --> 18:48.151
You want me to help?

18:48.153 --> 18:50.954
Well, I suppose I could
drop him on his head repeatedly.

18:50.956 --> 18:54.124
Okay, you know what,
I deserve that.

18:54.126 --> 18:56.139
Yesterday I said some
things that I regret.

18:56.140 --> 18:56.968
Mm. Like what?

18:56.992 --> 18:58.864
God, do we have
to do this now?

18:59.331 --> 19:00.597
Why not? I'm not going anywhere.

19:00.599 --> 19:02.999
Clearly, he's not
going anywhere.

19:03.001 --> 19:06.936
Okay, fine, I said that-that
you're not a very good father.

19:06.938 --> 19:09.005
And that is
simply not true.

19:09.007 --> 19:10.340
Thank you.

19:10.342 --> 19:12.342
That must have been
hard for you to say.

19:12.344 --> 19:15.211
And Jake is a very bright
and capable young man.

19:15.213 --> 19:17.947
And that must have been
damn near impossible to say.

19:19.117 --> 19:21.351
But... very sweet.

19:21.353 --> 19:23.987
Um, I shouldn't have gone
behind your back with Louis.

19:23.989 --> 19:26.956
But it just, it felt so good
that he wanted to be with me.

19:26.958 --> 19:29.025
And I've never been
anybody's first pick before.

19:29.027 --> 19:31.795
You were my first pick
to help me raise a kid.

19:31.797 --> 19:34.364
Clean up on aisle five.

19:34.366 --> 19:35.966
The floor's about to be
covered in tears.

19:35.967 --> 19:38.134
Okay. Can-Can you
give me a hand here?

19:40.205 --> 19:42.238
Okay, I've seen this
a million times before.

19:42.240 --> 19:45.141
There is one surefire parental
technique that always works.

19:51.049 --> 19:52.615
He wanted Froot Loops.

19:52.617 --> 19:54.984
We're good parents.
We really are.

19:54.986 --> 19:57.120
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:02.640 --> 20:04.574
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪
Louis is all tucked in.

20:04.898 --> 20:06.331
Oh, yeah?

20:06.333 --> 20:08.467
No extra
bedtime story?

20:08.469 --> 20:10.369
No secret dessert?

20:10.371 --> 20:12.738
No dancing like
no one's watching?

20:12.740 --> 20:15.941
No jazz hands were raised,
no heels were kicked.

20:15.943 --> 20:18.777
I appreciate that.
I got your back.

20:18.779 --> 20:21.213
And to say thank you,

20:21.215 --> 20:24.583
I got you a
special surprise.

20:26.386 --> 20:28.520
Froot Loops!

20:28.522 --> 20:30.913
Shh.
♪ Secret, secret ♪

20:30.914 --> 20:32.947
♪ We got a secret. ♪

20:33.502 --> 20:40.002
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
